Subject: [PATCH 08565/11362] [outer-loop] Phase 0c: fix graded-goal-bias
 exemplar capture and active-probe plan/pi reset

REQ-ARC-WMTE-6231 / REQ-ARC-WMTE-6232 (openspec/capabilities/arc-world-model-
trust-energy/spec.md), from the 2026-08-08 adversarial live-agent review.

_observe_level_boundary captured the CARNOT_ARC_GRADED_GOAL_BIAS win-state
exemplar from grid_of(latest) -- the frame RETURNED BY the winning action,
which for these games already shows the next level's opening board, not the
just-completed level's win state. That made the graded goal bias an inverted
gradient pulling search back toward the start instead of toward the goal.
Now prefers the last-admitted transition's PRE-action grid (Transition.grid,
not .next_grid), falling back to the old capture only if no transition has
been recorded yet.

_induce_and_plan now resets self.plan/self.pi to []/0 unconditionally at
entry, before any branch or early return. Under CARNOT_ARC_ACTIVE_PROBE=1, a
one-step probe plan leaves self.pi stale at 1 after it is consumed; a
subsequent reinduction (this function re-entered directly, bypassing the
normal level-boundary reset) installed a fresh plan without resetting pi, so
the policy either silently skipped the new plan's first step or raised
IndexError on a second one-step plan. Added a bounds guard on the induce
branch's direct _next_plan_move() call as defense in depth alongside the
reset.

New regression tests reproduce both defects against pre-fix source (verified
via git-stash comparison: 3 of 4 new tests fail on the old code, all 4 pass
on the fix) and the broader arc_competition_agent test surface (90 tests
across 7 files) stays green.

12 results/*.json artifacts carry freshness_acknowledgements entries for
this change. Both fixes are no-ops unless CARNOT_ARC_GRADED_GOAL_BIAS=1 or
CARNOT_ARC_ACTIVE_PROBE=1 is set: _induce_and_plan's body only ever WRITES
self.plan/self.pi after the reset line (grep-verified), and every dependent
artifact's generating script plus its own recorded config was grep-checked
clean for both flags. One second-order cascade entry, same shape as Phase
0b's, where acknowledging drift in two cited artifacts changed their hashes
and re-staled a third that cites them by content hash.

Committed with --only: the conductor's own concurrent git-add-A had staged
unrelated files (ops/conductor-log.md, several results/*.json, an in-flight
exp6220 pair) at commit time; --only restricts this commit to exactly the
paths listed below regardless of what else was staged in the index.

